          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong discrete space
            is, in general, an object of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+category"} concrete category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp
            of spaces that is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+functor"} free
            on its own underlying set. More generally, the notion can be applied relative to any
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A discrete space must, in particular, be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+object"} free object
            for the forgetful functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Sp
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\colon Sp\to Set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} left adjoint
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi Set
                    %mo →
                    %mi Sp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: Set \to Sp
            %em own
            underlying set; we must also require that the counit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mi U
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F U X\to X
            be an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          %p
            Thus, we say that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Sp
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\colon Sp \to Set
            (or more generally, any functor)
            %strong has discrete spaces
            or
            %strong discrete objects
            if it has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+functor"} fully faithful
            left adjoint. This ensures that the functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                  %mi Sp
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set \stackrel{F}\to Sp \stackrel{U}\to Set
          %p
            is (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} naturally isomorphic
            to) the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+functor"} identity functor
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Loc"} Loc
          %p
            Assuming that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faithful+functor"} faithful
            (as it is when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp
            is a concrete category), we can characterise a discrete space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            as one such that every function from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            (for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            any space) is a morphism of spaces. (More precisely, this means that every function from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(X)
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(Y)
            is the image under
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            of a morphism from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
          %p
            The dual notion is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codiscrete+object"} codiscrete object
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#discrete_geometric_spaces Discrete geometric spaces
          %p
            The best known example is a discrete
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subset"} open
            in the topology. This is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+topology"} discrete topology
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is discrete in this sense, then its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal+map"} diagonal map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta: X \to X \times X
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+map"} open
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta(X)
            is open, then so is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi i
                    %mi x
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_x^{-1}(\Delta(X)) = \{x\}
            for any
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_x(y) \coloneqq (x, y)
          %p
            This same space serves as a discrete object in many subcategories and supercategories of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convergence+space"} convergence space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} manifolds
            (because a discrete topological space has those properties).
          %p
            It is also
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sober+space"} sober
            and thus serves as a discrete
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame"} frame
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
            of
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CABA"} CABA
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Loc"} Loc
            is not concrete over
            = succeed ".)." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to X \times X
            is open and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to 1
            is also open. A locale that satisfies the latter condition is called
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overt+locale"} overt
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_0
            while every topological space is overt. Moreover, in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} classical mathematics
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/toposes"} toposes
          %p
            A discrete
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniform+space"} uniform space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            has all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflexive+relations"} reflexive relations
            as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entourages"} entourages
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covers"} covers
            as
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniform+cover"} uniform cover
          %p
            Strictly speaking, there is no discrete
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+space"} metric space
            on any set with more than one element, because the forgetful functor has no left adjoint. However, there is a discrete
            %em extended
            metric space, given by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(x,y) = \infty
            whenever
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \ne y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(x,y) = 1
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \ne y
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor+theorem"} adjoint functor theorem
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Met
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Met
            is that it generally lacks infinitary
            = succeed "s;" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ext
                  %mi Met
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ext Met
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Met
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Met_1
            are
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+category"} complete
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Abstract+Stone+Duality"} Abstract Stone Duality
            %strong discrete
            if the diagonal map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta: X \to X \times X
            is open, which corresponds to the existence of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equality
            relation on
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %em overt
            spaces in ASD.
          %h3#local_toposes Local toposes
          %p
            Any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+topos"} local topos
            has discrete and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codiscrete+object"} codiscrete
            objects. By definition, a local topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            comes with an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ↩
                        %mi coDisc
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi Γ
                    %mover
                      %mo ↩
                      %mi Disc
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{H}
                  \\stackrel{\overset{Disc}{\hookleftarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{\Gamma}{\to}}{\underset{coDisc}{\hookleftarrow}}}
                  \\mathbf{B}
          %p
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+topos"} base topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}
            (for instance
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Disc
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Disc
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Codisc
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Codisc
            are fully faithful. Thus, a
            %em discrete object
            is one in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essential+image"} essential image
            of the functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Disc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Disc
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            is not generally faithful in this case.
          %p
            Even more generally,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            may be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} local (∞,1)-topos
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} discrete ∞-groupoid
            \.
          %p
            Equivalently, this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
            induces an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+pair"} adjoint pair
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modalities"} modalities
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ♭
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mo ♯
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Disc
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi coDisc
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\flat \dashv \sharp)
                  \\coloneqq
                  ( Disc \Gamma \dashv coDisc \Gamma)
                  \\,,
          %p
            the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+modality"} flat modality
            and the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sharp+modality"} sharp modality
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+types"} modal types
            for the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+modality"} flat modality
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codiscrete+objects"} codiscrete objects
            are the modal types for the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sharp+modality"} sharp modality
          %h3#Fibrations Topological categories, fibrations, and final lifts
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+concrete+category"} topological concrete category
            has discrete (and also codiscrete) spaces
          %p
            More generally, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opfibration"} opfibration
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp
            has an initial object preserved by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp
            has discrete objects: the discrete object on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            can be obtained as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mo !
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_!(0)
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            is the initial object of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi ∅
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i\colon \emptyset \to X
            is the unique map from the initial object in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            (or whatever underlying category). (Conversely, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp
            has discrete objects and pushouts preserved by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is an opfibration.)
          %p
            Discrete objects can also be characterized as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/final+lifts"} final lifts
            for empty
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sinks"} sinks
          %h3#in_simplicial_sets In simplicial sets
          %p
            The category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+topos"} local topos
            (in fact a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+topos"} cohesive topos
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A
                %em discrete object
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
                is precisely the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
                of a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+groupoid"} discrete groupoid
            %li
              %p
                A
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codiscrete+object"} codiscrete object
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
                is precisely the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
                of a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codiscrete+groupoid"} codiscrete groupoid
          %h3#discrete_cellularcategorical_structures Discrete cellular/categorical structures
          %p
            Often one calls a cellular structure, such as those appearing in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
            %em discrete
            if it is in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essential+image"} essential image
            of the inclusion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
          %p
            For instance, one may speak of a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+category"} discrete category
            as a category that is equivalent (or, in some cases, isomorphic) to one which has only
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
            morphisms. This concept has a generalization to a notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+object+in+a+2-category"} discrete object in a 2-category
          %p
            An alternative terminology for this use of “discrete” is
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truncated+object"} 0-truncated
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+n-type"} homotopy 0-type
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-level"} 0-type
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+category"} topological category
            there is otherwise ambiguity in what it means to say that it is “discrete”: it could either mean that its underlying topological spaces (of objects and of morphisms) are discrete spaces, or it could mean that it has no nontrivial morphisms, but possibly a non-discrete topological space of objects.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              In some cases, the cellular notion of “discreteness” for higher categories can be seen as a special case of the
              %em spatial
              notion of discreteness — often the 1-category of shapes will have a functor to sets for which the cellularly discrete objects are the discrete objects in the sense considered on this page. For instance, this is the case for
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+topos"} local topos
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
          %h3#ExamplesInInfinityToposes
            In
            = succeed "-toposes" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            The definition of discrete objects has the evident generalization from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            to
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-category theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒳
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaf+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-sheaf (∞,1)-topos
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section"} global section
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi 𝒳
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo →
                      %mi Γ
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi Δ
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\Delta \dashv \Gamma)
                  \\colon
                  \\mathcal{X}
                  \\stackrel{\overset{\Delta}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{\Gamma}{\to}}
                  \\infty Grpd
          %p
            then for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝒳
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathcal{X}
            any object and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            any object, one says that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mi 𝒳
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H(X,A)
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\pi_0 \mathcal{X}(X,\Delta(A))
                  \\in
                  Set
          %p
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+with+constant+coefficients"} with (locally) constant coefficients
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒳
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}(-,-)
            denotes the
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categorical+hom-space"} (∞,1)-categorical hom-space
          %p
            Now if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒳
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}
            %em has discrete objects
            in the sense that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒳
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta \colon \infty Grpd \to \mathcal{X}
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} full and faithful (∞,1)-functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒳
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}
            equals the cohomology in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            = succeed "\u201D:" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒳
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi has
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi discrete
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi objects
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⇔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mo ∀
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∈
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi Grpd
                  %mi 𝒳
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Δ
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Δ
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\mathcal{X} \, has\, discrete\, objects)
                  \\Leftrightarrow
                  ( \forall_{S,A \in \infty Grpd} \mathcal{X}(\Delta S, \Delta A) \simeq \infty Grpd(S,A) )
                  \\,.
          %p
            Conversely:
            %em
              the failure of the cohomology with constant coefficients of objects in the image of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
              to coincide with standard cohomology is a measure for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
              not respecting discrete objects.
          %p
            For example the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+object"} natural numbers object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi N
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Δ
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{N} \simeq \Delta \mathbb{N}
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaf+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-sheaf (∞,1)-topos
            over some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            fails to be a discrete object. Accordingly in this case the natural numbers object can have nontrivial higher cohomology with constant coefficients, see for instance (
            %a{:href => "#Blass83"}> Blass 83
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Shulman13"} Shulman 13
